                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="620-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="620-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="620-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_hc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Hypercardioid" title="Hypercardioid" ><img id="620-3" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ><img id="620-4" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_wc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Wide Cardioid" title="Wide Cardioid" ></span>Microtech Gefell UMT 800</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The UMT800 is a multipattern FET condenser built around Gefell&#8217;s PVC-membrane M7 capsule. The mic has two diaphragms and a single, shared backplate. A switch on the microphone body allows selection of five different pickup patterns: cardioid, wide cardioid, omnidirectional, figure-8, hypercardioid.</p><p>Two recessed DIP switches on the mic body can selectively (and separately) enable a preattenuation pad (-10dB) and a high-pass filter (-10dB @ 90 Hz).</p><p>The UMT 800 ships with a mic clip (p/n EA 92) in a padded wooden storage case. Two finishes are available:</p><ul><li>Satin nickel (p/n  211104)</li><li>Dark bronze (p/n  211105)</li></ul><p></p><blockquote><p><cite>SoundOnSound</cite></p><p>the mic has a nominal 40Hz-18kHz frequency response, though there&#8217;s still a significant usable range above 18kHz, and the frequency response plots show a slight lift in the 10kHz region, which helps to give the sound a little air without introducing harshness. Interestingly, the presence peak is most pronounced in omni mode, with a 5 or 6dB rise at around 12kHz.</p></blockquote><p><p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Microtech-Gefell/UMT-800">Microtech Gefell UMT 800</a> is also known as: UMT800.</p>
